skill.prompt_template:
Debug Traefik with the following parameters:

Debug Configuration:
- Debug Target: {debug_target}
- Log Level: {log_level}
- Log Path: {log_path}
- Configuration Path: {config_path}
- Container Name: {container_name}
- Service Name: {service_name}
- Endpoint URL: {endpoint_url}
- Time Range: {time_range}
- Filter Pattern: {filter_pattern}
- Include Access Logs: {include_access_logs}
- Include Error Logs: {include_error_logs}
- Max Entries: {max_entries}

Diagnostic Context:
- Environment: {environment}
- Traefik Version: {traefik_version}
- Deployment Type: {deployment_type}

Diagnostic Steps:
1. Collect relevant logs within specified time range
2. Validate configuration syntax
3. Check service connectivity
4. Analyze health check status
5. Identify error patterns
6. Generate remediation recommendations

Error Handling:
- If log files inaccessible: report permissions issue
- If configuration invalid: provide specific syntax error location
- If service unreachable: report network diagnostic results
- If container not found: list available Traefik containers
- If timeout occurs: report partial results with timeout notice
